---
import PostLayout from '../../layouts/PostLayout.astro';
---

<PostLayout
  pageTitle="Into the Alps: Salzburg | Expeditions"
  heroTitle="Into the Alps:<br>Salzburg"
  heroSubtitle="Weekend getaway options in the Austrian Alps"
  seriesLabel="Into the Alps &mdash; Vol. II"
  heroStyle="background-image: url('https://media.bifunctional.xyz/expeditions/salzburg/04.jpg')"
  date="OCTOBER 9TH, 2021"
  location="Salzburg, Austria"
  footnote="Our weekend getaway to Salzburg occurred in the Fall of 2021 after quite an eventful two years. &copy; Zubin John"
  moreTitle="More Expeditions"
  description="A weekend in Salzburg: Untersberg, Hohensalzburg fortress, and the Sound of Music filming locations. October 2021."
  ogImage="https://media.bifunctional.xyz/expeditions/salzburg/04.jpg"
>
  <Fragment slot="nav-left">Into the Alps</Fragment>
  <a slot="nav-right" class="back-btn" href="/expeditions/">&#8592; All Expeditions</a>

  <style is:inline>
    .parallax-section{ position:relative; min-height:clamp(320px, 42vh, 420px); display:flex; align-items:center; background:center/cover no-repeat fixed; }
    .parallax-section::before{ content:""; position:absolute; inset:0; background:rgba(0,0,0,.42); }
    .parallax-inner{ position:relative; z-index:1; width:100%; max-width:var(--page); margin:0 auto; padding:0 var(--gutter); }
    .parallax-inner .text{ padding:0; }
    .parallax-section h3{ font-family:var(--sans); font-size:clamp(24px,3.3vw,38px); letter-spacing:.08em; font-weight:800; text-transform:uppercase; line-height:1.25; color:#fff; margin:0; }
    @media (max-width:768px){ .parallax-section{ min-height:clamp(260px, 36vh, 340px); background-attachment:scroll; } }
  </style>

  <!-- INTRO -->
  <section class="space-md">
    <div class="text">
      <p class="lede">
        Having arrived on a misty morning, Salzburg immediately delivered on its reputation as one of Central
        Europe's most dramatic small cities. Ringed by the Untersberg range and bisected by the Salzach, it is
        a place where baroque architecture, mountain terrain, and pop culture mythology exist in surprisingly
        close proximity.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- FULL IMAGE: 13, centred, no caption -->
  <section class="space-md">
    <div class="single">
      <figure>
        <div class="media"><img src="https://media.bifunctional.xyz/expeditions/salzburg/13.jpg" alt="Into the Alps: Salzburg photo 13" /></div>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- SECTION: UNTERSBERG -->
  <section class="space-sm">
    <div class="text">
      <h2 class="section-title">Journey to Untersberg</h2>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="space-sm">
    <div class="text">
      <p>
        Our first stop had to be the hulking Untersberg, right in the immediate vicinity of the city. With
        intermittent cloud cover and a fantastical funicular ascent, we made our way up to the summit. The
        mist made the peaks feel mystic and otherworldly, rolling in and out of the ridgeline.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 2+1: Untersberg (09, 08 top, 10 full width, tight rows) -->
  <section class="space-md">
    <div class="grid grid-2plus1" style="gap:8px;">
      <figure>
        <div class="media"><img src="https://media.bifunctional.xyz/expeditions/salzburg/09.jpg" alt="Into the Alps: Salzburg photo 9" /></div>
      </figure>
      <figure>
        <div class="media"><img src="https://media.bifunctional.xyz/expeditions/salzburg/08.jpg" alt="Into the Alps: Salzburg photo 8" /></div>
      </figure>
      <figure class="span-2">
        <div class="media"><img src="https://media.bifunctional.xyz/expeditions/salzburg/10.jpg" alt="Into the Alps: Salzburg photo 10" /></div>
      </figure>
    </div>
    <div class="text" style="margin-top:14px; padding-bottom:28px;">
      <figcaption>Mystic, shrouded peaks of the Untersberg range on a misty October morning.</figcaption>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- SECTION: HOHENSALZBURG -->
  <section class="space-sm">
    <div class="text">
      <h2 class="section-title">Fortress Hohensalzburg &amp; the Altstadt</h2>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="space-sm">
    <div class="text">
      <p>
        Right off the edge of the Salzburg Altstadt, walk to the Stiegkeller to ride the FestungsBahn up into
        the heart of the fortress. Once there, take in the panoramic views in every direction, stroll inside
        the fortress walls, and visit exhibits that transport you through the history of this European town.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 2+1: Hohensalzburg (01, 14 top, 03 full width, 12 and 05 row, then caption) -->
  <section class="space-md">
    <div class="grid grid-2plus1" style="gap:8px;">
      <figure>
        <div class="media"><img src="https://media.bifunctional.xyz/expeditions/salzburg/01.jpg" alt="Into the Alps: Salzburg photo 1" /></div>
      </figure>
      <figure>
        <div class="media"><img src="https://media.bifunctional.xyz/expeditions/salzburg/14.jpg" alt="Into the Alps: Salzburg photo 14" /></div>
      </figure>
      <figure class="span-2">
        <div class="media"><img src="https://media.bifunctional.xyz/expeditions/salzburg/03.jpg" alt="Into the Alps: Salzburg photo 3" /></div>
      </figure>
      <figure>
        <div class="media"><img src="https://media.bifunctional.xyz/expeditions/salzburg/12.jpg" alt="Into the Alps: Salzburg photo 12" /></div>
      </figure>
      <figure>
        <div class="media"><img src="https://media.bifunctional.xyz/expeditions/salzburg/05.jpg" alt="Into the Alps: Salzburg photo 5" /></div>
      </figure>
    </div>
    <div class="text" style="margin-top:14px;">
      <figcaption>Captivating vistas of Salzburg and its surroundings from the ramparts of Hohensalzburg.</figcaption>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="space-sm">
    <div class="text">
      <p>
        Back down in the heart of the Old Town, a short distance from the market you will find the charming
        little cemetery, Petersfriedhof, one of the oldest Christian burial sites in the German-speaking world.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 2+1: Old Town (06, 02 top, 07 full width, no caption) -->
  <section class="space-md">
    <div class="grid grid-2plus1" style="gap:8px;">
      <figure>
        <div class="media"><img src="https://media.bifunctional.xyz/expeditions/salzburg/06.jpg" alt="Into the Alps: Salzburg photo 6" /></div>
      </figure>
      <figure>
        <div class="media"><img src="https://media.bifunctional.xyz/expeditions/salzburg/02.jpg" alt="Into the Alps: Salzburg photo 2" /></div>
      </figure>
      <figure class="span-2">
        <div class="media"><img src="https://media.bifunctional.xyz/expeditions/salzburg/07.jpg" alt="Into the Alps: Salzburg photo 7" /></div>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- COVER QUOTE: Hohensalzburg (mint quote) -->
  <section class="cover-quote">
    <div class="cover-ph" style="background:linear-gradient(135deg, #2c3e50 0%, #1a2533 100%)"></div>
    <div class="inner">
      <figure>
        <p class="quote">Panoramic views in every direction, a leisured stroll inside the fortress.</p>
        <figcaption>Hohensalzburg Fortress, Salzburg, Austria</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- SECTION: SOUND OF MUSIC -->
  <section class="space-sm" style="padding-top:44px;">
    <div class="text">
      <h2 class="section-title">Ode to Hollywood</h2>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="space-sm">
    <div class="text">
      <p>
        No trip to Salzburg is complete without indulging in its most iconic tie to popular culture: the Sound
        of Music. A short bus ride outside the main city centre will bring you to Leopoldskron Palace, one of
        the two filming locations used for the Villa Trapp, home of the fictional Von Trapp family.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- GRID 2: Leopoldskron (11, 15) -->
  <section class="space-md">
    <div class="grid grid-2">
      <figure>
        <div class="media"><img src="https://media.bifunctional.xyz/expeditions/salzburg/11.jpg" alt="Into the Alps: Salzburg photo 11" /></div>
      </figure>
      <figure>
        <div class="media"><img src="https://media.bifunctional.xyz/expeditions/salzburg/15.jpg" alt="Into the Alps: Salzburg photo 15" /></div>
      </figure>
    </div>
    <div class="text" style="margin-top:14px;">
      <figcaption>Leopoldskron Palace, one of the filming locations for the Villa Trapp in The Sound of Music.</figcaption>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- PARALLAX: closing, 04 with text on top, directly above the location footer -->
  <section class="parallax-section" style="background-image:url('https://media.bifunctional.xyz/expeditions/salzburg/04.jpg')">
    <div class="parallax-inner">
      <div class="text">
        <h3>With that, our short day in Salzburg is at an end. Other must see spots include the Mirabell Gardens and Dom Quarter in Old Town.</h3>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- MORE CARDS -->
  <Fragment slot="more-cards">
    <a class="more-card" href="/expeditions/innsbruck/">
      <div class="more-thumb"></div>
      <p class="more-card-title">Into the Alps: Innsbruck</p>
      <span class="more-card-badge">Published &mdash; Oct 2021</span>
      <p class="more-card-sub">Altstadt, Nordkette, and Castle Ambras</p>
    </a>
    <a class="more-card" href="/expeditions/verona/">
      <div class="more-thumb"></div>
      <p class="more-card-title">Verona</p>
      <span class="more-card-badge">Published &mdash; Oct 2020</span>
      <p class="more-card-sub">Of Bridges and Brawls</p>
    </a>
    <a class="more-card" href="/expeditions/bangkok/">
      <div class="more-thumb"></div>
      <p class="more-card-title">Bangkok Airwaves</p>
      <span class="more-card-badge">Published &mdash; Mar 2019</span>
      <p class="more-card-sub">Wat Pho, Wat Arun, Phra Nakhon district</p>
    </a>
  </Fragment>
</PostLayout>
